[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="WeaponResource" load_steps=4 format=3 uid="uid://cmbrvlhuntingbow"]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Combat/WeaponResource.cs" id="1_weapon"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://src/Combat/Actions/ActionDefinitionResource.cs" id="2_action"]

; The first ranged weapon in the game (2026-09-05). Everything structural about it is shared with a
; sword — the same resource type, the same action timeline, the same equipment socket — and the only
; difference is what happens on the release frame: an arrow leaves instead of a volume opening.
;
; ONE link, not a chain. A bow does not combo: each shot is drawn, loosed and recovered on its own,
; and the pressure comes from the draw being long enough that you have to choose when to start it.
; 0.86 s of draw out of a 1.35 s shot is deliberate — long enough to be committed to, short enough
; that a second shot is a real option when something is running at you.
;
; ⚠️ NO WARP. A ranged action must never close distance on its target; that is the whole difference
; between a bow and a charge, and RootMotion stays None for every ranged definition.

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="Loose"]
